author: codex
estimated_minutes: 240
acceptance_criteria: Package and lock resolve @unbrained/pm-cli and pm-changelog 2026.8.7; peer compatibility starts at 2026.8.7; pm merge install emits extensions/** -merge and the managed manifest pm-json exception; no any or dynamic/inline imports are introduced; npm and Bun release gates pass with exact 100/100/100 coverage and zero skipped tests; a packed artifact activates against a fresh tracker using the installed pm CLI; current tracked files and reachable history are scanned for privacy and identity blockers; exact-head Actions and available bot reviews are dispositioned before merge; no npm publication occurs without maintainer approval
definition_of_ready: Canonical main is clean and current at v2026.08.07; one active checkout plus this bounded worktree exists; GitHub and package trackers contain no duplicate open work; installed global pm is 2026.8.7
value: Keep the canonical TypeScript SDK reference aligned with the exact contracts agents consume
impact: Prevents generated extension assets from crossing concurrent branches through semantic PM merges and removes dependency drift
outcome: "A reviewed package-owned compatibility tranche with reproducible npm, Bun, coverage, privacy, and installed-CLI evidence"
why_now: The companion fleet audit leaves pm-ts-starter as one of three packages missing the 2026.8.7 fence
reviewer: maintainer
risk: high
confidence: high
sprint: 2026-08-compatibility
release: Unreleased
resolution: "Updated the current pm toolchain and peer floor, installed the 2026.8.7 merge fence, migrated the lifecycle guard from authored JavaScript to fully tested erasable TypeScript, and validated npm, Bun, coverage, packaging, privacy, and fresh-tracker activation."
expected_result: "The TypeScript reference package consumes current pm contracts, protects generated extension state across concurrent branches, and passes reproducible package and installed-CLI verification without conflating merge readiness with publication readiness."
actual_result: "Package and lock resolve pm CLI/SDK and pm-changelog 2026.8.7; peer floor is 2026.8.7; the canonical extension fence is installed; the authored prepare hook is erasable TypeScript with fail-loud broken-CLI behavior and Windows PATH/PATHEXT absence detection; npm and Bun release gates pass with 134 tests, zero skips, exact 100/100/100 for three source files, zero production vulnerabilities, and deterministic packaging/changelog checks; a packed tarball activated all nine capabilities in a fresh pm 2026.8.7 tracker, preserved the one-item native list, reported the exact SDK target, and ran hello; current tracked files and all-history secret-shape scans are clean. Independent items preserve history privacy, missing quality gates, and legacy tracker cleanup. No publication occurred."
