notes[4]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-07T17:55:46.918Z",codex,"Fresh packed-artifact acceptance used global pm 2026.8.7 in a newly initialized Git tracker. Installation activated the package in project scope with all nine declared capabilities and no blocking health findings; pm list returned exactly the fixture item,ts-starter info reported version and SDK target 2026.8.7,hello returned Hello,Agent,and pm validate had no warnings."
  "2026-08-07T17:55:46.918Z",codex,"Privacy audit: current tracked host-path and secret-shape scans returned zero. Reachable history has two non-noreply identities among five unique identities and 69 revisions with absolute host-path shapes; pm-ts-starter-t5xx blocks publication pending maintainer-approved rewrite. The all-history secret-shape scan returned zero."
  "2026-08-07T18:03:31.800Z",codex,"Review round 1: Greptile correctly identified that npm's Windows executable is a pm.cmd shim requiring shell handling; the installer now selects pm.cmd with shell enabled only on win32 and has an exact command-shape regression test. CodeRabbit correctly required command-qualified history reproduction steps and found three stale README SDK references; both were corrected through append-only PM mutation and current/version-neutral documentation."
  "2026-08-07T18:08:56.905Z",codex,"Review round 2: Greptile correctly identified that shell-mediated Windows absence returns a status rather than ENOENT. The lifecycle now resolves the npm shim against Windows PATH/PATHEXT before execution,treating no matching file as the intended consumer-install no-op while preserving fail-loud behavior for a located broken command; deterministic tests cover quoted paths,extension normalization,absence,and execution."
